%% 2026-04-10 extension for predict_interview_qa
%% New additive outputs: company_dossier, interview_risk_map, confidence_breakdown, reliability_state.
%% The existing three-tab UI and SQLite-backed prediction table remain unchanged.
%% Lightweight crawl stays same-domain first, with safe caps and no JS/PDF default.
%% The Interview Q&A detail view renders company_dossier and interview_risk_map from normalized payloads when available.
%% Prediction rows expose Recall/Edit, which reloads stored input snapshot data when available so operators can edit and rerun a prior submission.
%% Automation run logs are created early, and log viewer fallback uses stored run detail when the file path is stale.
%% Interview crawl canonicalizes www/non-www same-domain matching to keep redirecting company sites in the same coverage bucket.
%% Generation prompt carries dossier summaries plus page titles and URLs to strengthen company understanding when multiple public pages are available.
%% 2026-04-11 update: date-triggered pending runs and schedule overrides now use a short misfire grace window so minor sync delay does not drop queued runs.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now defaults to a shorter LLM timeout so unresponsive local model calls fail fast and fall back sooner.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now synthesizes a grounded heuristic payload on model timeout so the run can complete without a second blocking vet call.
%% 2026-04-11 update: the generation prompt is compacted to reduce token pressure and lower Ollama latency in the hot path.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now uses a 20-second model timeout with no retry loop so fallback activates quickly instead of compounding latency.
%% 2026-04-11 update: predict_interview_qa now separates intent and proof bundles before generation so the final pack keeps one interview angle per question when possible.
%% 2026-04-11 update: a rule-based dedup pass drops repeated answer skeletons and moves low-uniqueness questions into gap/drill items instead of persisting template-like duplicates.
%% 2026-04-12 update: Reposts Analytics now includes Stack Trends, which classifies jobs into stack groups and surfaces crawl recommendations for thin buckets.
%% 2026-04-12 update: Stack Trends reuses the same cached external source pattern as Language Trends so broader world context stays off the hot path.
%% 2026-04-12 update: stale external market context now returns cached data immediately and refreshes in the background instead of blocking the analytics chart.
%% 2026-04-12 update: trend AI snapshots are now refreshed nightly and persisted to SQLite so page load only reads the DB snapshot.

